    "message": {
     "content": "### Verdict: Yes, This is a Very Strong Offer \u2014 Accept It\n\nThis is a massive win. You leveraged your unvested equity perfectly: Google met you on base salary, held the initial $1.08M equity grant, and handed you a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus**. \n\nBy giving you the $200k in upfront cash, Google effectively bought out your next 12 months of Meta vesting dollar-for-dollar **on top** of granting you a full new-hire equity package.\n\n---\n\n### Compensation Comparison (Final Offer vs. Meta)\n\n| Component | Meta (IC6 PM) | Google Final Offer (L6 PM) | Delta / Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | Match |\n| **Target Bonus** | ~$36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | **+$12,000** |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | $0 | **$200,000** | **+$200,000** (Upfront Cash) |\n| **Initial GSU Grant (Yr 1)** | ~$200,000 (Unvested) | ~$356,400 *(33% front-loaded)*<br>*(or $270,000 if flat 25%)* | **+$70,000 to +$156,400** |\n| **Year 1 Total Comp** | **~$526,000** | **~$758,000 \u2013 $844,400** | **+44% to +60% increase** |\n\n---\n\n### What Makes This Offer Compelling\n\n1. **Guaranteed Cash Arbitrage in Year 1:**  \n   You were worried about walking away from $200,000 of Meta RSUs that were subject to stock price volatility. Google is replacing that with **$200,000 in liquid cash**, while still granting you $1.08M in GSUs starting from Day 1.\n2. **Top-Tier L6 Banding:**  \n   $240k base + $1.08M GSU + $200k sign-on puts your Year 1 compensation near the top 5\u201310% percentile for L6 Product Managers in the Bay Area.\n3. **True Best-and-Final:**  \n   A $200k sign-on bonus at L6 is near the ceiling of what compensation committees approve without an L7 down-leveling or a competing written offer.\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Year Outlook (The \"Sign-On Cliff\")\n\nBe mindful of how your compensation trajectory looks over the next 3\u20134 years so you aren't surprised by the Year 2 drop:\n\n* **Year 1:** **~$760k \u2013 $844k** *(Boosted by the $200k sign-on)*\n* **Year 2:** **~$644k+** *(Base + Bonus + 33% GSU + Year 1 refresh)*\n* **Year 3:** **~$550k \u2013 $600k** *(GSU drops to 22%, but 2 years of stacked refreshes kick in)*\n* **Year 4:** **~$520k \u2013 $580k** *(GSU drops to 12%, but 3 years of stacked refreshes kick in)*\n\nEven with the sign-on dropping off after Year 1, your average annualized compensation over the 4-year cycle will significantly outpace staying at Meta on your current trajectory unless Meta promoted you to IC7 immediately.\n\n---\n\n### Checklist Before You Sign\n\nBefore formally accepting, clarify these two procedural points with your recruiter:\n\n1. **Sign-on Payout & Clawback Terms:** Confirm whether the $200k is paid in a single lump sum on your first or second paycheck (standard) and verify the clawback window (typically 12 months, occasionally prorated across 24 months).\n2. **Vesting Schedule:** Confirm if your offer uses Google\u2019s standard front-loaded schedule (**33% Year 1, 33% Year 2, 22% Year 3, 12% Year 4**) or the flat 25%/year schedule. Front-loaded maximizes your Year 1/2 liquidity.\n\n### Final Recommendation\nSince compensation is your primary driver, **accept the offer**. You successfully turned a lateral proposal into a top-tier package with a massive first-year cash premium.",
